<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n484" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăchĕlōŭs</span></b> ,
		i, m., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχελῶος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A celebrated river of Middle Greece</i>, <i>which</i>, <i>rising in Pindus</i>,
				<i>separates Aetolia from Acarnania</i>, <i>and empties into the Ionian Sea</i>, now the <i>Aspropotamo</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3,
				10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 1, 2 al.</span></i>—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The river-god Achelous</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 8,
				549 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 8</span></i> sq.; <i><span class="en">Prop.
				2, 34, 33 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
